course: dictionary
lesson: 8348
title: Rooster and its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A rooster is a male chicken. You can work out its meaning from the clues around it: it has a bright red comb, colourful tail feathers, and it crows loudly in the morning. «Some roosters attack people to protect their hens, so you walk away calmly and tell the owner.» Here, rooster must be a bird that guards the hens, so it is a male chicken.
explain: Try the swap check. Put «male chicken» into the sentence instead of rooster: «Some male chickens attack people to protect their hens.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Other words in the same family help too. The female is a hen, and the babies are chicks. In the UK, a male chicken may also be called a cockerel.
fact: A rooster is an adult male chicken. A hen is the female.
fact: Roosters crow loudly, often at dawn, which is how a farm wakes up.
fact: «A chicken egg takes about 21 days to hatch if kept warm.» The babies that hatch are called chicks.
fact: Rooster is also the name of one animal in the Chinese zodiac. It comes after Monkey and before Dog.
fact: The zodiac animals go round in order, so the same animal comes back every 12 years.
exercise: «The rooster crowed at dawn, waking the whole farm.» What does rooster mean? | A kind of farm gate | A female chicken | *A baby chick | A male chicken
exercise: «The rooster and the hen sat on the fence.» Which word means the female chicken? | *hen | sat | fence | rooster
exercise: In the Chinese zodiac, which animal comes just before Rooster? | *Monkey | Pig | Dog | Goat
test: What should you do if a rooster comes at you on a farm? | Feed it all the food you have | *Walk away calmly and tell the owner | Hit it with a stick | Run and shout loudly
test: What are the babies of a hen and a rooster called? | Cubs | Calves | *Chicks | Kittens
exam: «A rooster crows at dawn.» What time of day does a rooster usually crow? | *Dawn | Dusk | Noon | Midnight
